[Music]  6 41 here on a wednesday morning it is  time once again for our morning cup of  joe's segment we are joined live by  metro sheriff joe lombardo  sheriff good to see you once again  thanks for joining us this morning  appreciate it  good morning john it's good to see you  in the studio i know somehow they let me  back in for a change  let's talk about the the news of the day  the news of the last couple of weeks  we saw the ride on capitol hill in  washington d.c last week  the las vegas sun reported yesterday  that metro police was  investigating whether officers from here  in in las vegas  were over in washington during that  event can you talk about the  investigation  and what's being done at a department  level to look into this  yeah i think it's a similar uh proactive  step that  all the police departments across the  nation are taking uh  because i think it's important for us in  law enforcement to have that sense of  objectivity and you know people have  their first amendment right to do what  they want to do but in that case  uh it went beyond that and so i think  it'd be troublesome for  an individual to be part of the law  enforcement community  knowing that they entered the capital  and did  insurrection is the word being used  today  and it's important for us to  identify an individual if they did that  and do whatever we can to remove them  from  the law enforcement community  it it i support what they  what people want to do but obviously in  this case it just went beyond  desire to protest versus becoming a riot  are you aware of any officers that did  uh go into the capitol  no as of today no um but we're working  hand in hand with the fbi  and we're going through all the videos  and relying on people to call in if they  know  um and we'll do an intensive follow-up  if  in fact we do identify somebody kind of  jumping off of that we heard from  federal authorities that they're  prepared for possible  large demonstrations on inauguration day  in state capitals obviously that's up in  carson city but  uh what is metro doing uh just to  prepare uh here in southern nevada for  what might happen next week  yeah you know and it's unfortunate that  we're already prepared for  these type of incidents um you know  during the summer time with the  uh protests associated with george floyd  and everything else and  we've been dealing with in society in  the last few months  to include covet and what i mean by that  unfortunately we've had plenty of  practice  with the people out protesting doing  their first amendment rights and  everything else that goes along with it  but in this case  there was a warning obviously the  president said what he said  and individuals weren't prepared and  that's my opinion i believe law  enforcement was  ill-prepared to deal with the situation  that took place and so now we have a  warning  we we're aware that there may be  interesting  occurring here on the 20th and we're  putting people in place and plans in  place to  to address it accordingly and so after  that event  in dc in proximity and during that event  in dc we did deploy troops here to the  local courthouse federal courthouse and  the state capitol  so we've had sufficient warning  associated with it and  it's a failure of leadership if we do  not respond to that warning  and i believe that's what happened in  washington d.c  um sheriff let's switch gears quickly to  coronavirus vaccines you and i have  talked before about the effect of covet  on the department uh from top to bottom  will you require officers to get a  vaccination and get immunized  uh well first and foremost uh thank you  for asking the question  because there is always a concern with  your first responders  becoming victims of the virus so to just  put it in perspective i've had  over a thousand employees to date uh  since march of last year um that have  come back positive for  cobit so we're dealing with that as a  workforce and a labor  issue and all the contact tracing that  goes along with it and  people gone on a daily basis and doing  what we're  paid to do and fighting crime so moving  forward the vaccines available  they made it in us in the first tier  as far as going to get the initial shot  and then subsequently the second shot  so it is it's voluntary um i guess  that's the core of your question  it's voluntary at this point because of  collective bargaining and everything  else that you could imagine  but up until the vaccine  was available it was presumptive that  you if you were positive you received it  at work and we took care of your time  off  and now as we move forward with the  vaccine being available it's no longer  presumptive  and so we're encouraging our employees  to go get the vaccine  so we can ensure that we continue to be  a viable  and robust workforce so it's a  three-phase attempt for us  for the first responders office  commission officers and the  corrections officers in the jail are  first to go and then it's the follow-up  of the rest of the police officers in  the second phase and the third phase  will be our civilian employees  and we have a suspense date of april  first for the second shot to be  completed  okay so it's it's encouraged but not  required just because of collective  bargaining  i think we have time to quickly sneak in  a quick question about dui crashes in  the valley we've seen  some relatively high profile ones can  you just talk quickly about the effort  to fight the issue here as we start the  new year have things been improving  recently since the holidays  well since the holidays no  it's actually been had we've had a  significant increase in fatal accidents  associated with uh  dui in the first month of the year of  the calendar year  but if you look at compared to 19 versus  20  of last year we had a 11 decrease in  fatal accidents associated with dui  so that's positive but we're  experiencing a significant increase here  in the first month  more people are driving people are  getting back to work  no matter how many times we preach it  you know dui is bad and you have all the  options  of uber and lyft and everything else um  it seems to still be happening which is  troublesome to me  personally and for the community um so  we have to continue to fight the fight  and educate people  and do uh enforcement whenever possible  to try to curb the  this particular issue all right well  sheriff we will certainly keep an eye on  that we appreciate you joining us this  morning and answering our questions take  care and we'll catch up with you later  if you have a question for sheriff  lombardo you can always submit it online  just head to 8newsnow.com  you can find out if your question is  answered every wednesday 6 4

